  "scope": "An actual finite constructor traverses the original represented vertex spine to allocate its own shared canonical rational zero row, then hands that exact returned row to a real graph-context assembler. The same-run result is the literal original GlobalContext with retained enumeration, directed matrix and source/target words. The complete physical run uses 5*n+38 successful instructions and n+14 allocated cells and includes the paid terminal halt bound. No zero row or assembled graph context is supplied. Actual kept-matrix and shortest-path composition, original input representation and initial physical address widths remain explicit.",
